# Gemini API key for the LIVE doubt tutor (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey).
# Without it the app still runs - the doubt session uses a scripted stub.
#
# This is a STUDENT-FACING key and is deliberately not the authoring key in
# /.env.example: students type real questions into this one, and free tiers
# train on what they are sent. Link billing before a child's text reaches it.
#
# The in-class voice is Gemini Live (gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview) over
# Google's own WebSocket - OpenRouter serves text only, so it cannot carry it.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter key for the TYPED doubt tutor (https://openrouter.ai/keys).
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. Every VITE_ value is inlined into the JavaScript the
# browser downloads, so this key is readable by anyone who opens devtools on a
# deployed build - and an OpenRouter key with no credit limit is a key someone
# else can spend. Set a credit limit on it while it lives here, and move both
# keys behind a server before this app is deployed anywhere public.
# When set it wins over the Gemini key above, which is what keeps typed doubts
# working while a Google project is blocked. It cannot carry the live VOICE -
# OpenRouter serves text only - so speaking to her still needs VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY.
VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE BACKEND THE APP TALKS TO
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase project. Both are PUBLIC — the anon key is a published identifier,
# and what a student may read or write is decided by row-level security on the
# server, never by hiding this. The service key, which IS a secret, never comes
# near a browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Where the relays live.
#
# BLANK IN DEV, and that is the normal setting: the paths stay relative and the
# vite dev server answers them with the same code the deployed function runs.
#
# In production, the deployed Edge Function's base:
#   https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/relay
# Public — it is a URL, and every relay behind it checks who is asking.
VITE_RELAY_URL=
